{
  "name": "01 - Support Ticket Classifier",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Setup checklist after import\n1. Create credential **OpenAI API** (or swap the Chat Model node for Azure OpenAI) — used by 'OpenAI Chat Model' and 'OpenAI - Draft Auto Reply'.\n2. Create credential **Postgres** — host `postgres`, db/user/password from your `.env` — used by 'Postgres - Insert Ticket'.\n3. Make sure `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` is set in `.env` (restart the n8n container after editing), or swap the HTTP Request nodes for the native Slack node.\n4. Run `sql/init.sql` once against Postgres to create the `tickets` table.\n5. Activate the workflow, then test:\n```\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:5678/webhook/support-ticket \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"customerId\":\"CUST-1001\",\"message\":\"Our main office has had zero internet connectivity since 9am, this is urgent.\"}'\n```",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 420
      },
      "id": "cb62485c-9917-4dfb-82b4-51afb30f8984",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -816,
        544
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "support-ticket",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "02831c8b-7fe9-4e27-a5f2-84dc682d2e7d",
